Bugfix: Manage focus and announce state for the header menus

Opening the app menu or the user menu with the keyboard left the focus
sitting on the toggle instead of moving into the menu, and screen readers
had no way to tell whether the menu was open or closed: it carried neither
aria-expanded nor aria-haspopup. Pressing Escape had no effect while a menu
was open, so keyboard users who tabbed in had no way back out except by
clicking.

The toggle now announces its expanded state, opening the menu moves focus
to its first entry, and Escape closes the menu again from the entry or the
toggle - the focus returns to the toggle only when it was still inside the
menu when it closed. Action menus in the file list are unaffected, since
they do not go through this code path.

WCAG 2.1 AA, SC 2.4.3, SC 4.1.2
